Hi Chris,

Thanks so much for your response! I'm very grateful that you are so active on here and so helpful! :D

However, I was afraid of that being your answer. Is there a way to do it after the UDs are already calculated? I am calculating a HR for each cat in winter and summer for several years, so I have 187 home ranges already created. I did these in a batch for each site, and it took several hours to run them all :D I would love to not have to re-run all that code! I just finished writing some code that brings all the AKDE results back in from saved lists and creates the polygons for the 95% UDs, rasterizes the density surface from the PMF, and pulls the area of the UD from summary() so I can look at the differences in HR size and intensity of use between season_years for each individual. But, ideally, I would also like to calculate the pairwise overlap between HRs from summer to winter or from year to year to help identify shifts over time.  Any way to do this without rerunning everything?

Thanks again for your help!!

On Friday, September 22, 2023 at 5:19:34 PM UTC-6 Christen Fleming wrote:
> Hi Kristin,
>
> The easiest way to calculate your UDs in the same grid is to calculate them in one call like akde(TELEMETRY_LIST,FIT_LIST). This will work fine as long as the home ranges aren't radically different sizes.
>
> Best,
> Chris
>
> On Friday, September 22, 2023 at 4:44:31 PM UTC-4 Kristin Engebretsen wrote:
> > Hi Chris,
> >
